    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "READ FIRST - experiment and checks",
      "pos": [
        1600,
        1230
      ],
      "size": [
        970,
        760
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Two-video Omni blend\nUpload one video in A and another in B. Describe each clip in its own prompt box; <Video 1> means that branch's clip. All media inputs start empty.\n\nContext mix blends Qwen text and visual embeddings; reference latent mix blends VAE video references. Ratios use 0=A, 1=B. Keep the seed fixed. Compare (0,0), (1,1), (0.5,0), (0,0.5), and (0.5,0.5), then try the same video and prompt in both branches.\n\nFor animated reference mixing choose sine, triangle, linear, or an easing curve. The live preview shows the B ratio over reference time. Context mix stays constant. Reference timing does not pin generated frames and is not a denoising-step schedule.\n\nBoth clips load from their first frame at 24 fps, up to 124 frames, resized to 768 x 768. Short clips hold their final frame. Output starts at 1024 x 1024, 124 frames. References travel through conditioning; the sampler starts from an empty AV latent.\n\nVERIFY MIX reports actual tensor interpolation, token truncation/padding, and tag mismatches. There is no semantic token or motion alignment. A owns the token layout. Midpoint interpolation can produce double exposures or distortion. Audio references are disconnected; generated audio follows the blended context.\n\nSelect matching Ref2VA model/LoRA files on your installation. Eight Euler/simple steps, shifts 12/3, and SageAttention are enabled. See the pack README for dependencies and how to bypass optional SageAttention or tiny-VAE preview nodes.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Two-video Omni blend\nUpload one video in A and another in B. Describe each clip in its own prompt box; <Video 1> means that branch's clip. All media inputs start empty.\n\nContext mix blends Qwen text and visual embeddings; reference latent mix blends VAE video references. Ratios use 0=A, 1=B. Keep the seed fixed. Compare (0,0), (1,1), (0.5,0), (0,0.5), and (0.5,0.5), then try the same video and prompt in both branches.\n\nFor animated reference mixing choose sine, triangle, linear, or an easing curve. The live preview shows the B ratio over reference time. Context mix stays constant. Reference timing does not pin generated frames and is not a denoising-step schedule.\n\nBoth clips load from their first frame at 24 fps, up to 124 frames, resized to 768 x 768. Short clips hold their final frame. Output starts at 1024 x 1024, 124 frames. References travel through conditioning; the sampler starts from an empty AV latent.\n\nVERIFY MIX reports actual tensor interpolation, token truncation/padding, and tag mismatches. There is no semantic token or motion alignment. A owns the token layout. Midpoint interpolation can produce double exposures or distortion. Audio references are disconnected; generated audio follows the blended context.\n\nSelect matching Ref2VA model/LoRA files on your installation. Eight Euler/simple steps, shifts 12/3, and SageAttention are enabled. See the pack README for dependencies and how to bypass optional SageAttention or tiny-VAE preview nodes.\n"
      }
    },
